harness/db/schema.sql-715--- THE REVIEW-TO-VERSION CHAIN (Sol build gate 3, 2026-07-20).
harness/db/schema.sql-716---
harness/db/schema.sql-717--- Sol's most dangerous flaw: "approve version A, builder changes it to B, the old
harness/db/schema.sql-718--- approval still counts — believable green checks on code nobody reviewed."
harness/db/schema.sql-719---
harness/db/schema.sql-720--- The fix is not another approval ceremony; it is arithmetic. A verdict carries the
harness/db/schema.sql-721--- version it reviewed. A job carries the version it is putting forward. Completion
harness/db/schema.sql-722--- guards only count verdicts whose versions MATCH — so moving the code voids the
harness/db/schema.sql-723--- approvals by construction, nothing needs to remember to revoke anything. And a
harness/db/schema.sql-724--- FAIL condemns the version it saw, not the job forever: fix the code, the version
harness/db/schema.sql-725--- changes, the old fail becomes history. (A fail with no recorded version blocks
harness/db/schema.sql-726--- everything — fail-closed, because it condemned we-don't-know-what.)
harness/db/schema.sql-727--- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
