harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-6--- schema counted distinct SEATS (guard_full_panel) and required a higher TIER
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-7--- (guard_local_output_needs_review), but never counted FAMILIES. So the property
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-8--- this whole project exists to guarantee rested on Python being correct.
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-9---
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-10--- Now the DB refuses ->done unless at least `required_review_families` DISTINCT
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-11--- families have a PASSING reviewer verdict on the CURRENT version. The floor is
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-12--- snapshotted per job at dispatch (like required_reviews) and cannot be lowered.
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-13---
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-14--- RECOVERY-SAFE (Sol re-gate, 2026-07-20): an earlier edit to schema.sql, re-run by
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-15--- init_db() on server restart, installed these two triggers WITHOUT the column they
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-16--- reference — jamming every status change on the live DB. So this migration DROPs the
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-17--- triggers first, adds the column, backfills in-flight jobs to the real floor, then
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-18--- recreates the triggers — all in one transaction. Runs once, on a pre-005 DB.
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-19-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-20-BEGIN;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-21-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql:22:DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS guard_family_floor;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql:23:DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS guard_family_floor_is_fixed;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-24-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-25-ALTER TABLE jobs ADD COLUMN required_review_families INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-26-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-27--- Terminal rows stay 0 (history is history). Jobs still IN FLIGHT get the real floor so
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-28--- they can't slip to done under the old one-family rule (Sol: don't grandfather active
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-29--- work). They park until a real cross-family panel can satisfy the floor — the safe wait.
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-30-UPDATE jobs SET required_review_families = 2
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-31- WHERE status NOT IN ('shipped', 'failed', 'cancelled', 'done');
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-32-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-33--- The floor cannot be lowered after dispatch (mirrors guard_panel_size_is_fixed).
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql:34:CREATE TRIGGER guard_family_floor_is_fixed
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-35-BEFORE UPDATE OF required_review_families ON jobs
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-36-WHEN OLD.required_review_families > 0 AND NEW.required_review_families < OLD.required_review_families
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-37-BEGIN
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-38-    SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'guard: the family floor cannot be lowered after dispatch');
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-39-END;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-40-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-41--- The floor itself: >= N distinct families with a PASSING reviewer verdict on THIS
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-42--- version. Counts families (not seats, not roles other than reviewer), version-matched
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-43--- so moving the code voids old passes. Fails closed: too few families -> parked.
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql:44:CREATE TRIGGER guard_family_floor
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-45-BEFORE UPDATE OF status ON jobs
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-46-WHEN NEW.status = 'done' AND OLD.status <> 'done' AND NEW.required_review_families > 0
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-47-BEGIN
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-48-    SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'guard: fewer model families reviewed this than required')
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-49-    WHERE (
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-50-        SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT v.model_family) FROM verdicts v
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-51-        WHERE v.job_id = NEW.id AND v.verdict = 'pass' AND v.role = 'reviewer'
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-52-          AND v.reviewed_version IS NEW.head_version
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-53-    ) < NEW.required_review_families;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-54-END;
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-55-
harness/db/migrations/005_family_floor_2026-07-20.sql-56-COMMIT;
