harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-4--- Found by diffing the live DB against a fresh build of schema.sql on 2026-07-20:
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql:5:--   1. guard_verdicts_cannot_be_deleted   MISSING — a failing review could be deleted,
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-6---      then the job completed (Sol round 3, verified exploit).
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-7---   2. guard_no_approval_is_born_granted  MISSING — an approval could be inserted
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-8---      pre-granted, skipping the read-back guards (Sol round 3, verified exploit).
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-9---   3. guard_full_panel                   STALE — live version counts any 'pass',
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-10---      so testers/verifiers could fill the reviewer panel (Sol round 2, #5).
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-11---   4. jobs.tier / jobs.tier_reason       MISSING — tiering has nowhere to record.
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-12---   5. seats model_/effort_ tier columns  MISSING — same.
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-13---
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-14--- Additive ALTERs + trigger recreation only. No row is rewritten or re-inserted —
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-15--- replaying history through the guards is exactly what the guards exist to prevent.
harness/db/migrations/001_harden_live_db_2026-07-20.sql-16--- Backup taken first: harness/db/backups/chief.db.pre-hardening-2026-07-20
