harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-5---
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-6--- Jobs now carry head_version (the exact content hash being put forward); verdicts
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-7--- carry reviewed_version (what the reviewer actually looked at). Completion guards
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-8--- only count verdicts whose version MATCHES, so moving the code voids approvals by
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-9--- construction, and a fail condemns the version it saw instead of the job forever.
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-10---
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-11--- Existing rows keep NULL versions: job 1 shipped before versioning existed (its
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-12--- record is history and stays untouched); job 2 cannot now complete until it gets a
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-13--- version and version-matched reviews — which is correct, nobody reviewed a
harness/db/migrations/002_review_version_chain_2026-07-20.sql-14--- recorded version of it.
