harness/db/schema.sql-381-
harness/db/schema.sql-382--- The safe set. Everything an agent needs to actually build software, and nothing
harness/db/schema.sql-383--- that can hurt you. Note what ISN'T here — that's the whole point.
harness/db/schema.sql-384-CREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS safe_capabilities AS
harness/db/schema.sql-385-SELECT 'read_code' AS capability UNION ALL SELECT 'write_worktree'
harness/db/schema.sql:386:UNION ALL SELECT 'run_tests' UNION ALL SELECT 'open_pr';
harness/db/schema.sql-387-
harness/db/schema.sql-388--- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
harness/db/schema.sql-389--- APPROVALS — a signed, single-use permission slip for ONE exact dangerous act.
harness/db/schema.sql-390---
harness/db/schema.sql-391--- Sol on why a "yes" cannot be trusted on its own:
--
harness/db/schema.sql-482-
harness/db/schema.sql-483--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
harness/db/schema.sql-484--- Events: the live activity stream. What an agent is doing RIGHT NOW.
harness/db/schema.sql-485---
harness/db/schema.sql-486--- This is what makes the text channel feel like the Claude Code terminal — you
harness/db/schema.sql:487:-- watch Riggs read auth.py, edit routes.py, run pytest, and come back green.
harness/db/schema.sql-488--- Without it the harness can only tell you a job "happened," which is useless
harness/db/schema.sql-489--- while you're waiting and only mildly interesting afterward.
harness/db/schema.sql-490---
harness/db/schema.sql-491--- ONE STREAM, TWO RENDERINGS (this is the key design decision):
harness/db/schema.sql-492---   VOICE reads jobs.spoken_summary — a sentence. "Riggs is on it, two minutes."
--
harness/db/schema.sql-501--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
harness/db/schema.sql-502-CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS events (
harness/db/schema.sql-503-    id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
harness/db/schema.sql-504-    job_id        INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
harness/db/schema.sql-505-    seat_id       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES seats(id),
harness/db/schema.sql:506:    lane          TEXT NOT NULL,             -- 'riggs' | 'finn' | 'nova' | 'forge' ...
harness/db/schema.sql-507-    model         TEXT NOT NULL,             -- who is actually in the chair right now
harness/db/schema.sql-508-    family        TEXT NOT NULL,
harness/db/schema.sql-509-    -- 'skipped' is load-bearing (task #10): the record needs a word for something that
harness/db/schema.sql-510-    -- did NOT happen. A reviewer that was capped out or couldn't run must leave a mark,
harness/db/schema.sql-511-    -- or a panel that quietly shrank looks identical to a full one. (Migration 006.)
--
harness/db/schema.sql-524--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
harness/db/schema.sql-525--- Artifacts: GROUND TRUTH. Captured by the harness, not reported by a model.
harness/db/schema.sql-526---
harness/db/schema.sql-527--- This is the anti-fabrication layer, and it exists for a specific reason:
harness/db/schema.sql-528--- GPT-5.6-sol's own system card admits it fabricates results, and METR measured a
harness/db/schema.sql:529:-- cheating rate higher than any public model they'd evaluated. A tester that lies
harness/db/schema.sql-530--- doesn't just fail — it silently disables the only quality gate in the fleet,
harness/db/schema.sql:531:-- because nothing checks the tester.
harness/db/schema.sql-532---
harness/db/schema.sql-533--- The defense is structural: Playwright drives the app like a real user and the
harness/db/schema.sql-534--- HARNESS writes the screenshots, traces, console logs and network dumps to disk.
harness/db/schema.sql:535:-- The tester never asserts "I ran it and it worked" — it INTERPRETS artifacts it
harness/db/schema.sql:536:-- did not produce and cannot forge. You can't fabricate a screenshot.
harness/db/schema.sql-537---
harness/db/schema.sql:538:-- Forge (the existing Claude Code integration tester) already worked this way by
harness/db/schema.sql-539--- discipline: "If you didn't execute it and see it work, it's not tested."
harness/db/schema.sql-540--- Here that stops being a personality trait and becomes a constraint.
harness/db/schema.sql-541--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
harness/db/schema.sql-542-CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS artifacts (
harness/db/schema.sql-543-    id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
--
harness/db/schema.sql-776-    SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'guard: a reviewer cannot misrepresent its own tier or family');
harness/db/schema.sql-777-END;
