harness/gatekeeper.py-277-    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
harness/gatekeeper.py-278-    # ORDER IS THE POINT: the RECORD decides first, the irreversible act happens
harness/gatekeeper.py-279-    # second. Merging and then asking produced "the code merged but the record wouldn't
harness/gatekeeper.py-280-    # accept it" — an unreviewed merge with a polite note. The gatekeeper's own checks
harness/gatekeeper.py:281:    # are a SUBSET of the schema's (it never checks for a passing tester), so the only
harness/gatekeeper.py-282-    # safe order is to let the schema refuse before git is touched at all.
harness/gatekeeper.py-283-    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
harness/gatekeeper.py-284-    with _MERGE_LOCK:
harness/gatekeeper.py-285-        # Re-resolve under the lock and merge the SHA, never the name. Between the check
harness/gatekeeper.py-286-        # above and `git merge refs/heads/<branch>`, a builder could move the branch;
