docs/sol/sol_round2.out:14:You have reviewed this system four times and found serious weaknesses each time — nine flaws in the database rules, then eighteen more, then the finding that the "capability gate" was ineffective because it governed the record rather than the action, and in round 4 the deepest finding yet: an agent can put a harmful payload into its working copy, fool the model reviewers, receive genuine passing records, and have the release service deliberately deploy it — no forgery required, every door working exactly as designed. You rejected the design and listed 12 required changes, three of which were owner decisions.
docs/sol/sol_round2.out:19:- The owner (Neill — NON-TECHNICAL, cannot read code) has personally decided the three questions you made conditions of approval: (A) he ACCEPTED mandatory human written sign-off for high-authority change classes, with everything else autonomous; (B) agents run in a dedicated VM on this Mac, migratable to separate hardware later; (C) the PHI-bearing EMR is OUT of scope now, revisitable only after strict egress controls are built and attack-tested.
