docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-95-*legal* way to use the Claude Max subscription (Anthropic bans subscription OAuth in third-party
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-96-tools) — and it is exactly the path that costs 3–5s per turn.**
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-97-
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-98-> **You cannot have both "Claude Max subscription" and "snappy voice head." They are mutually
--
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-116-  agentic tool-calling, no CoT overhead, subscription already held — *but its TTFT is unverified and
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-117-  load-bearing*); (2) **Claude Haiku 4.5** via direct API (~1.04s, best TTFT consistency — needs API
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-118-  billing, not the Max sub); (3) **GPT-5.6 at `none`/`low` effort** (OpenAI's own guidance names
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-119-  `low` for latency-sensitive work — but same family as the 13s number, so verify).
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md:120:- **Explicitly NOT the head:** GPT-5.6-sol at high/max, Claude Fable, **anything behind `claude-cli`.**
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-121-- **Dispatch targets (Reasoners):** GPT-5.6-sol high/max via Codex; Claude Opus/Fable via
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md:122:  `claude-cli`; Grok Build; Ollama. All spawned non-blocking via `sessions_spawn` with explicit
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-123-  per-spawn `model`. Their multi-second startup is irrelevant in the background.
