harness/db/schema.sql-142-    id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
--
harness/db/schema.sql-262-    --             the gauntlet IS the approval; Neill gates production DEPLOYS, not
harness/db/schema.sql-263-    --             merges). Guard 6 still requires a cross-family tester on the record.
harness/db/schema.sql-264-    -- (Earlier wording — "only Neill can move this" — predates Decision D.)
harness/db/schema.sql-265-    -- These are NOT the same thing, and conflating them is how agents launder
harness/db/schema.sql:266:    -- confidence. From Chief's memory, learned the hard way:
harness/db/schema.sql-267-    --     "Chief must NEVER say 'shipped' unless Neill has confirmed it works on
harness/db/schema.sql-268-    --      his device. 'Shipped' is reserved for Neill-confirmed-working."
harness/db/schema.sql-269-    -- That rule now lives here instead of in a prompt.
harness/db/schema.sql-270-    status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'todo'
--
harness/db/schema.sql-273-    -- Set ONLY by the owner, through mark_shipped(). No agent has a path to this.
harness/db/schema.sql-274-    owner_confirmed_at TEXT,
harness/db/schema.sql-275-
harness/db/schema.sql-276-    -- How many passing reviews this job needs before it may complete. Set at
harness/db/schema.sql:277:    -- dispatch from the gauntlet config. Also from Chief's memory:
harness/db/schema.sql-278-    --     "Full set, always. No 'minimum,' no 'pick two,' no 'optional depending
harness/db/schema.sql-279-    --      on scope.'"
harness/db/schema.sql-280-    required_reviews INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
harness/db/schema.sql-281-
--
harness/db/schema.sql-493---   TEXT  reads THIS table in full   — every tool call, every file, every result.
harness/db/schema.sql-494--- Same truth, different verbosity. The voice can escalate into this table on
harness/db/schema.sql-495--- request ("what's it actually doing?") — see [voice] in seats.toml.
harness/db/schema.sql-496---
harness/db/schema.sql:497:-- Note `lane` and `model` are BOTH recorded. The lane (Riggs) carries the memory
harness/db/schema.sql-498--- and the conventions; the model is whoever is sitting in that chair today. You
harness/db/schema.sql-499--- must always be able to see which — otherwise you can't tell whether your auth
harness/db/schema.sql-500--- module was built by your best coder or your cheapest one.
harness/db/schema.sql-501--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
