docs/sol/sol_round5.out-736-    55	### 4.4 Escalation reviewer — Claude (Max subscription + credit pool)
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-737-    56	- Two modes, and the distinction matters:
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-738-    57	  - **Interactive (subscription, effectively free):** Neill opens a Claude Code session (locally or via SSH) and reviews the gauntlet's flagged queue himself with Claude. Human-initiated = subscription limits.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:739:    58	  - **Headless (credit pool):** the harness may invoke `claude -p` for automated deep reviews, drawing on the Max plan's included monthly agent credits. Budget-cap this in config (e.g., N automated Claude reviews/day) so it never silently overruns the free allotment.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-740-    59	- Role: highest-judgment work — architecture review, contested reviewer verdicts, the bug the local model looped on three times.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-741-    60	- This seat is optional/droppable. The system must run fully without it.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-742-    61	
