docs/sol/sol_round5.out-746-    65	## 5. Voice layer (the product)
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-747-    66	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-748-    67	### 5.1 The core architecture decision — voice skin ≠ brain
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:749:    68	The voice layer and the orchestrator are **separate**. A fast, local voice front-end handles listening and speaking; it makes **tool calls** to the GPT-5.6 orchestrator (Codex, §4.1) which holds the harness memory, subagents, and reasoning. You are talking *to your actual orchestrator* — the local pipeline is just its ears and mouth. This is what kills the Chief Command latency wound: the voice layer acknowledges in ~300ms ("on it, kicking that off") while 5.6 reasons and builds underneath. Perceived latency is the voice layer's, not the builder's.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-750-    69	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-751-    70	This means you get 5.6's full intelligence — interrogating a build, pushing back, inspecting its own work — with local, free, low-latency voice on top. The orchestrator is never a dumbed-down voice model; it's the real brain with all the context and subagents.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-752-    71	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-753-    72	### 5.2 Interaction model
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-781-   100	- Codex does not auto-spawn custom agents — delegation must be written explicitly into the workflow prompts / AGENTS.md.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-782-   101	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-783-   102	## 7. Memory & state
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-784-   103	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:785:   104	- Port Neill's existing memory files (CLAUDE.md / MEMORY.md-style markdown) into a harness-level `memory/` directory loaded into orchestrator context.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-786-   105	- Session state, job queue, and build history in SQLite on the host.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-787-   106	- Every dispatched job gets a persistent record: what was asked, which provider ran it, gauntlet verdicts, final status. Voice query "what did the overnight run do?" must be answerable from this.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-788-   107	- Git as audit trail for everything the agents produce.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-789-   108	
--
