docs/sol/sol_round5.out-874-    53	question was never "which vendor" — it's "how hard is the thing you're talking to trying to think."
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-875-    54	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-876-    55	### The design flaw
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-877-    56	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:878:    57	§5.1 has the voice layer tool-calling "the GPT-5.6 orchestrator which holds the harness memory,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-879-    58	subagents, and reasoning." **That routes every voice turn through a deep reasoning model** — even
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-880-    59	"what did the overnight run do?" The spec then papers over it with a canned ~300ms "on it, kicking
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-881-    60	that off" while the slow model grinds. That's a bandaid on a design problem.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-882-    61	
