docs/sol/sol_round5.out-904-    83	### ⚠️ The landmine — this kills the Claude Max head, and possibly the whole subscription premise
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-905-    84	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-906-    85	**CLI-based runtimes cannot be in a per-turn voice loop:**
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-907-    86	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:908:    87	- `claude -p` subprocess: **3–5s overhead per call.** Cited discussion says this makes "use cases
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-909-    88	  like voice assistants **prohibitively slow**."
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-910-    89	- Claude Agent SDK `query()`: **~12s overhead per call**, no hot-process reuse
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-911-    90	  ([claude-agent-sdk-typescript#34](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/issues/34)).
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-912-    91	- With process pre-warming/reuse: drops to <1s. Without it, you eat the full cost **every turn**.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-913-    92	- Direct Messages API: 1–3s end-to-end.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-914-    93	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:915:    94	This collides head-on with the constraint from §1: **`agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` is the only
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-916-    95	*legal* way to use the Claude Max subscription (Anthropic bans subscription OAuth in third-party
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-917-    96	tools) — and it is exactly the path that costs 3–5s per turn.**
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-918-    97	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-919-    98	> **You cannot have both "Claude Max subscription" and "snappy voice head." They are mutually
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-937-   116	  agentic tool-calling, no CoT overhead, subscription already held — *but its TTFT is unverified and
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-938-   117	  load-bearing*); (2) **Claude Haiku 4.5** via direct API (~1.04s, best TTFT consistency — needs API
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-939-   118	  billing, not the Max sub); (3) **GPT-5.6 at `none`/`low` effort** (OpenAI's own guidance names
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-940-   119	  `low` for latency-sensitive work — but same family as the 13s number, so verify).
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:941:   120	- **Explicitly NOT the head:** GPT-5.6-sol at high/max, Claude Fable, **anything behind `claude-cli`.**
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-942-   121	- **Dispatch targets (Reasoners):** GPT-5.6-sol high/max via Codex; Claude Opus/Fable via
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:943:   122	  `claude-cli`; Grok Build; Ollama. All spawned non-blocking via `sessions_spawn` with explicit
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-944-   123	  per-spawn `model`. Their multi-second startup is irrelevant in the background.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-945-   124	
