docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1189-   364	  background-recording app reports a subset of users **routinely get recordings killed** by the
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1190-   365	  watchdog. They stripped the entire view hierarchy on background to get CPU to 0% in the profiler,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1191-   366	  saw "massive improvements," and **still see background terminations.** Apple publishes **no CPU or
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:1192:   367	  memory thresholds** for what survives.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1193-   368	- **Picovoice's own FAQ hedges:** background wake-word "is controlled by the operating system, and
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1194-   369	  Picovoice **cannot guarantee** that this will be possible in future releases of iOS."
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1195-   370	- Every phone call, Siri invocation, or app grabbing the mic is an interruption you must catch and
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1196-   371	  recover from — and recovery is not always granted. User swipes the app away → dead, nothing
