docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1256-   431	  `workspace`, `tools` profile, `identity`. All four providers natively supported:
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1257-   432	  - **Codex** — supported, but a distinct runtime path (`codex` plugin + native app-server harness). Fiddliest of the four; budget real time.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1258-   433	  - **Grok/xAI** — supported; SuperGrok OAuth is the documented recommended path (subject to the tier trap above).
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1259-   434	  - **Ollama** — supported, auto-detected at `127.0.0.1:11434`.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:1260:   435	  - **Claude headless** — supported via `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` (reuses `claude -p` under your own session auth). This is the escalation seat.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1261-   436	- **The dispatcher** = native subagents (`sessions_spawn`). Non-blocking, returns a run id,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1262-   437	  and **each spawn takes an explicit `model` param** — so one orchestrator turn fans out across
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1263-   438	  Grok + Ollama + Claude simultaneously. `maxConcurrent` default 8; `maxSpawnDepth` 2 is the
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1264-   439	  documented orchestrator pattern. **Do not build a custom dispatcher.**
