docs/sol/sol_round4.out-164-- No shared folders, clipboard, or device passthrough; no credential connections; no
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-165-  host-management channel; no Tailscale identity inside; no inbound connections.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-166-- Outgoing traffic only through the named brokers, enforced by a host-side firewall the
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-167-  guest cannot reconfigure.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out:168:- Fixed-size disk; hard CPU, memory, process, time, and network limits — an agent must
docs/sol/sol_round4.out:169:  not be able to brick the Mac by exhaustion. Disk-full/memory/flood/crash responses
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-170-  tested.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-171-- Isolated clones per agent — never shared working copies (a git worktree shares
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-172-  history and hooks; a clone doesn't).
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-173-- The profile covers every runner (Claude Code, Codex, Ollama), child process, hook,
