docs/sol/sol_round4.out-379-   spend, contact, reveal. The missing boundary against code that passes review — deploy
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-380-   permission ≠ the authority the code gets after it starts.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-381-4. **Make the release path exclusive.** Production accepts ONLY packages signed through
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-382-   this chain; disable every old deploy script, automation identity, admin bypass.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out:383:5. **Complete trusted package chain.** Agent submits a restricted patch (never a built
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-384-   package); a clean builder builds, signs, stores immutably; production verifies the
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-385-   signature before starting it.
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-386-6. **Egress as architecture, not slogan.** Enforcement outside the agent and production
docs/sol/sol_round4.out-387-   workloads; per-project/per-provider rules; admit generic scanning can't stop encoded
