docs/sol/sol_round1.out-690-question was never "which vendor" — it's "how hard is the thing you're talking to trying to think."
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-691-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-692-### The design flaw
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-693-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:694:§5.1 has the voice layer tool-calling "the GPT-5.6 orchestrator which holds the harness memory,
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-695-subagents, and reasoning." **That routes every voice turn through a deep reasoning model** — even
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-696-"what did the overnight run do?" The spec then papers over it with a canned ~300ms "on it, kicking
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-697-that off" while the slow model grinds. That's a bandaid on a design problem.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-698-
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-720-### ⚠️ The landmine — this kills the Claude Max head, and possibly the whole subscription premise
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-721-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-722-**CLI-based runtimes cannot be in a per-turn voice loop:**
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-723-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:724:- `claude -p` subprocess: **3–5s overhead per call.** Cited discussion says this makes "use cases
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-725-  like voice assistants **prohibitively slow**."
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-726-- Claude Agent SDK `query()`: **~12s overhead per call**, no hot-process reuse
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-727-  ([claude-agent-sdk-typescript#34](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/issues/34)).
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-728-- With process pre-warming/reuse: drops to <1s. Without it, you eat the full cost **every turn**.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-729-- Direct Messages API: 1–3s end-to-end.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-730-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:731:This collides head-on with the constraint from §1: **`agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` is the only
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-732-*legal* way to use the Claude Max subscription (Anthropic bans subscription OAuth in third-party
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-733-tools) — and it is exactly the path that costs 3–5s per turn.**
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-734-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-735-> **You cannot have both "Claude Max subscription" and "snappy voice head." They are mutually
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-753-  agentic tool-calling, no CoT overhead, subscription already held — *but its TTFT is unverified and
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-754-  load-bearing*); (2) **Claude Haiku 4.5** via direct API (~1.04s, best TTFT consistency — needs API
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-755-  billing, not the Max sub); (3) **GPT-5.6 at `none`/`low` effort** (OpenAI's own guidance names
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-756-  `low` for latency-sensitive work — but same family as the 13s number, so verify).
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:757:- **Explicitly NOT the head:** GPT-5.6-sol at high/max, Claude Fable, **anything behind `claude-cli`.**
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-758-- **Dispatch targets (Reasoners):** GPT-5.6-sol high/max via Codex; Claude Opus/Fable via
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:759:  `claude-cli`; Grok Build; Ollama. All spawned non-blocking via `sessions_spawn` with explicit
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-760-  per-spawn `model`. Their multi-second startup is irrelevant in the background.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-761-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-762-### 🔬 Spike C (new, and it gates the architecture)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-763-
