docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1975-- **Duplicate protection** so a retry can't start the same job twice.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1976-- **Reviews tied to the exact version tested.**
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1977-- **Crash recovery** — reconcile jobs after power loss, sleep, network failure, OpenClaw
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1978-  restart.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:1979:- **Tested backups** of job history and memory.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1980-- **Real authentication on the phone app.** Being on the tailnet is not proof of being
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1981-  Neill.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1982-- **Prompt-injection defence** — malicious instructions hidden in code, web pages,
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-1983-  issues, dependencies, test output.
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2206-Chief is not one thing with one access level. He's **three layers**, each with
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2207-different permissions:
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2208-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2209-1. **Voice/chat LLM** — the thing that talks to you. Reads a system prompt
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2210:   you've seen (agent roster, memory files, project context). Runs on the
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2211-   Anthropic API. Has no hands.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2212-2. **Voice/chat LLM with project-switch detection** — same LLM, but the
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2213-   server-side handler can update `current_project` based on your
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2214-   utterance. That's the most it can change.
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2217-   is the layer with real hands. Full filesystem write within the scoped
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2218-   repo. Full git. Full `gh`. Full pytest. Full anything you have installed.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2219-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2220-The security story is that **layers 1 and 2 are read-only + routing**, and
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2221:**layer 3 is scope-gated + env-restricted**. Everything interesting lives at
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2222-layer 3.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2223-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2224----
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2225-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2226-## Layer 1: Voice/chat LLM (read-only, always-on)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2227-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2228-### Reads
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2229-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2230:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user/memory/*.md` (your global user + feedback
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2231:  memory, always loaded)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2232:- `~/.claude/agents/memory/*.md` (Chief's own agent roster — Atlas, Forge,
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2233-  Riggs, Finn, Nova, Vera, Hawke, Sable, Pax, Quill, Hip, names + roles)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2234:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user-Desktop-<scope>/memory/*.md` (**only** the
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2235:  currently-scoped project's memory, exact canonical match, no substring
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2236-  leaks)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2237-- Conversation history within the current WebSocket session
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2238-- Project scope set via the picker or voice command
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2239-
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2249-  defaults stay cheap because heavy lifting moves to layer 3.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2250-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2251-### Risks
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2252-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2253:- **Prompt injection from memory files.** Memory files are concatenated into
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2254-  the system prompt. A compromised sub-agent writing to one could hijack
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2255-  Chief's behavior. Mitigation: identity-prompt guard text, provenance
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2256:  fences around each file (`<memory file="…" mtime="…">…</memory>`), and
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2257-  file-source tagging so odd instructions are visible.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2258:- **Symlink read.** Someone dropping a symlink at `~/.claude/.../memory/`
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2259-  to `~/.ssh/id_rsa` would get it read into Chief's context and sent to
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2260-  Anthropic. Mitigation: symlink rejection at read time (implemented in
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2261:  `memory_paths.safe_md_files` + `team_service`/`memory_service`).
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2262-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2263----
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2264-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2265-## Layer 2: Project-switch detection
