docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2403-## What Chief voice itself can write (future v1.1)
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2404-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2405-Two options we're evaluating for direct-write capability:
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2406-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2407:1. **`append_to_memory(scope, filename, content)` tool** — Chief voice has
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2408-   a bounded tool that appends to scope-matching `.md` files. Scope-gated
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:2409:   (can't write Arch memory while scoped to Chief Command). No path
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2410-   traversal, no creation of new filenames outside a whitelist pattern.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2411-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2412-2. **Dispatch everything.** Memory edits go through `claude` subprocess,
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-2413-   meaning a full audit trail + ability to review edits before they land.
--
