docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5551-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5552-    -- 'done'    = the gauntlet passed. The machine is satisfied.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5553-    -- 'shipped' = NEILL said it works on his device. Only he can move this.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5554-    -- These are NOT the same thing, and conflating them is how agents launder
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:5555:    -- confidence. From Chief's memory, learned the hard way:
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5556-    --     "Chief must NEVER say 'shipped' unless Neill has confirmed it works on
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5557-    --      his device. 'Shipped' is reserved for Neill-confirmed-working."
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5558-    -- That rule now lives here instead of in a prompt.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5559-    status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'todo'
--
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5562-    -- Set ONLY by the owner, through mark_shipped(). No agent has a path to this.
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5563-    owner_confirmed_at TEXT,
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5564-
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5565-    -- How many passing reviews this job needs before it may complete. Set at
docs/sol/sol_round1.out:5566:    -- dispatch from the gauntlet config. Also from Chief's memory:
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5567-    --     "Full set, always. No 'minimum,' no 'pick two,' no 'optional depending
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5568-    --      on scope.'"
docs/sol/sol_round1.out-5569-    required_reviews INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
