docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-1-# Codex bridge for Chief Command — 2026-08-27
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-2-
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-3-**What Neill asked for:** "the same thing as Arch for Chief" — open a terminal, start a
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md:4:Codex session, and Codex knows the project, has its own queue of work and its own memory
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-5-of what it did, and runs its own reviewer gauntlet.
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-6-
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md:7:**What it is:** three plain files and three scripts. There is no memory *system*; the
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md:8:memory is the queue ("what next") and the worklog ("what I did"), re-read from disk each
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-9-session. AGENTS.md is the contract Codex reads on startup (Chief already had this — its
docs/CODEX_BRIDGE_2026-08-27.md-10-CLAUDE.md is literally `@AGENTS.md`, so one file binds both harnesses).
