docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-327-**Phase 1 — Text harness (the machine).**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-328-OpenClaw daemon on MacBook Pro; Codex OAuth connected; Ollama serving a local model; web UI reachable from phone over Tailscale. ✅ *Accept: from the phone, type "have the local model write X, then have Codex review it" and it happens, with the job recorded.*
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-329-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-330-**Phase 2 — Voice loop, local, wired to the orchestrator.**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:331:Whisper + Kokoro + Pipecat pipeline on the desktop client, making tool calls into the GPT-5.6 orchestrator with full harness memory. ✅ *Accept: push-to-talk at desk, talk through a build with the orchestrator (not a stand-in), hear the answer begin in <1.5s while heavy work runs underneath.*
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-332-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-333-**Phase 3 — Voice from phone.**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-334-PWA push-to-talk over Tailscale. ✅ *Accept: from the golf course parking lot, dispatch a build by voice and hear confirmation.*
