docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5325-## 1. Spec corrections (do these first)
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5326-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5327-| # | Spec claim | Verdict | Action |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5328-|---|---|---|---|
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5329:| 1 | Claude headless `claude -p` draws from a Max-plan **monthly agent-credit pool** (§4.4) | **WRONG** — announced, then **paused before taking effect**. Anthropic's own support article: *"We're pausing the changes… For now, nothing has changed."* `claude -p` draws on normal subscription limits. | Delete §4.4's credit-pool mechanics and the budget-cap-as-necessity framing. Keep headless usage *isolated* as forward-proofing (Anthropic says it will re-propose with notice). **Do keep** the real constraint: subscription OAuth tokens in third-party tools are prohibited (terms Feb 20 2026, billing enforcement Apr 4 2026). |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5330-| 2 | Codex subagents: **up to 8 parallel workers** (§4.1) | **WRONG** — `agents.max_threads` **defaults to 6**. The "8" looks like contamination from the Grok Build claim. (`max_depth = 1` and the `~/.codex/agents/` TOML layout are **correct**; GA March 2026 **confirmed**.) | Fix fan-out arithmetic to 6, or set `max_threads` explicitly and validate empirically. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5331-| 3 | Codex OAuth for third-party harnesses is **"sanctioned by OpenAI"** (§4.1) | **WRONG as stated.** It *works* — it's what OpenClaw's OpenAI provider uses — but no OpenAI doc sanctions it, and OpenAI's ToS forbids sharing account credentials / programmatic extraction outside permitted surfaces. It is **tolerated, not sanctioned**. | **This is the biggest latent risk in the spec.** See §5 below. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5332-| 4 | OpenAI realtime voice ~$0.18–0.46/min → $700–1000/mo (§5.3) | **WRONG — off by ~10×.** See **§1c**, which supersedes this row. Real figure at Neill's usage: **~$25/mo (mini), ~$76/mo (full).** The architectural half (not in the subscription; separate metered billing) is CONFIRMED. Model name stale (`-2.1`). | **The sole stated justification for the local voice stack has collapsed.** Re-litigate on true numbers. Also kill the "realtime = GPT-5.6" premise — it's a distilled family with a Sept-2024 cutoff. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5333-| 5 | Google/Gemini excluded — ToS bans third-party OAuth (names OpenClaw), consumer CLI dead June 18 2026 (§4.5) | **CONFIRMED, both halves.** ToS names OpenClaw explicitly; mass bans were *enforced* Feb 2026; consumer access ended June 18. | No change. §4.5 is correct. |
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5362-question was never "which vendor" — it's "how hard is the thing you're talking to trying to think."
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5363-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5364-### The design flaw
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5365-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5366:§5.1 has the voice layer tool-calling "the GPT-5.6 orchestrator which holds the harness memory,
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5367-subagents, and reasoning." **That routes every voice turn through a deep reasoning model** — even
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5368-"what did the overnight run do?" The spec then papers over it with a canned ~300ms "on it, kicking
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5369-that off" while the slow model grinds. That's a bandaid on a design problem.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5370-
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5392-### ⚠️ The landmine — this kills the Claude Max head, and possibly the whole subscription premise
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5393-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5394-**CLI-based runtimes cannot be in a per-turn voice loop:**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5395-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5396:- `claude -p` subprocess: **3–5s overhead per call.** Cited discussion says this makes "use cases
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5397-  like voice assistants **prohibitively slow**."
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5398-- Claude Agent SDK `query()`: **~12s overhead per call**, no hot-process reuse
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5399-  ([claude-agent-sdk-typescript#34](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/issues/34)).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5400-- With process pre-warming/reuse: drops to <1s. Without it, you eat the full cost **every turn**.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5401-- Direct Messages API: 1–3s end-to-end.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5402-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5403:This collides head-on with the constraint from §1: **`agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` is the only
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5404-*legal* way to use the Claude Max subscription (Anthropic bans subscription OAuth in third-party
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5405-tools) — and it is exactly the path that costs 3–5s per turn.**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5406-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5407-> **You cannot have both "Claude Max subscription" and "snappy voice head." They are mutually
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5425-  agentic tool-calling, no CoT overhead, subscription already held — *but its TTFT is unverified and
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5426-  load-bearing*); (2) **Claude Haiku 4.5** via direct API (~1.04s, best TTFT consistency — needs API
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5427-  billing, not the Max sub); (3) **GPT-5.6 at `none`/`low` effort** (OpenAI's own guidance names
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5428-  `low` for latency-sensitive work — but same family as the 13s number, so verify).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5429:- **Explicitly NOT the head:** GPT-5.6-sol at high/max, Claude Fable, **anything behind `claude-cli`.**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5430-- **Dispatch targets (Reasoners):** GPT-5.6-sol high/max via Codex; Claude Opus/Fable via
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5431:  `claude-cli`; Grok Build; Ollama. All spawned non-blocking via `sessions_spawn` with explicit
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5432-  per-spawn `model`. Their multi-second startup is irrelevant in the background.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5433-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5434-### 🔬 Spike C (new, and it gates the architecture)
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5435-
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5516-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5517-### Other things that bite
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5518-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5519-- **Hard 60-minute session cap.** A 2-hour builder session needs ≥2 reconnects with context
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5520:  rehydration — and a fresh session means a **cold cache** (cost spike + a memory seam). Needs
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5521-  design, not hand-waving.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5522-- **Prompt caching is load-bearing, not an optimization.** Without it the context-replay term goes
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5523-  from $0.168/hr → **$13.44/hr**. That is the entire difference between "cheap" and "unusable."
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5524-  Requires a stable prefix — never interpolate timestamps into the system prompt.
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5635-|---|---|
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5636-| **PWA, background / locked screen, wake word** | 🔴 **IMPOSSIBLE.** Not hard — *impossible.* iOS suspends PWAs shortly after backgrounding; service workers get only narrow event-driven windows and **cannot** do continuous audio ([WebKit #211018](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=211018)). State this to the owner without hedging. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5637-| **PWA, foreground, phone mounted, open mic** | ✅ **WORKS TODAY. This is the 90% answer.** Tap once on entering the car, then talk freely the whole drive, with barge-in. Add **Wake Lock API** to keep the screen awake. ~**a day of work, mostly deleting PTT logic.** Gotcha: use a single-page shell with **no hash routing** — iOS standalone-mode `getUserMedia` re-prompts on navigation ([WebKit #185448](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=185448), [#215884](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=215884)). |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5638-| **Siri App Intent as launcher → hands off to our session** | ⭐ **THE SLEEPER. Best effort-to-payoff ratio.** *"Hey Siri, ask Chief…"* works **hands-free, screen locked, phone in pocket**, needs **no special entitlement and no wake-word engine** — Siri gives us the system-level wake word for free, then our app takes over the mic and runs the full open-mic Realtime session. Requires a thin native shell. Ceiling (inferred): Siri is a *launcher*, not a host — you don't run a Realtime session inside Siri's voice loop. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5639:| **Native app + Porcupine + `UIBackgroundModes: audio`** | ✅ Achievable. True custom *"hey Chief"*, screen off, in-pocket. **Sideloading removes the App Store constraint entirely** — `UIBackgroundModes: audio` is a *normal capability*, not a restricted entitlement. No review, no rejection risk. Costs: a real native app, a wake-word integration, and a **persistent red mic dot in the status bar** (cannot be suppressed). |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5640-| **CarPlay** | 🔴 **HARD BLOCKER. CUT IT.** iOS 26.4 *did* add exactly the right category (voice-based conversational apps, built for ChatGPT/Gemini-class assistants) — but **CarPlay entitlements are Apple-granted per-category, case-by-case, and cannot be self-signed.** No personal provisioning profile can carry one. Apple granting a one-man internal tool a conversational-AI CarPlay entitlement is ~zero. Also: Apple is explicitly *not* handing the wake-word slot to third parties — Siri stays the system assistant in CarPlay. |
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5641-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5642-#### 🔧 Owner data point: the Archie app (real prior experience, and it corrects the above)
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5643-
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5672-- **[Apple Forums #776055](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/776055):** a *shipping* native
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5673-  background-recording app reports a subset of users **routinely get recordings killed** by the
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5674-  watchdog. They stripped the entire view hierarchy on background to get CPU to 0% in the profiler,
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5675-  saw "massive improvements," and **still see background terminations.** Apple publishes **no CPU or
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5676:  memory thresholds** for what survives.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5677-- **Picovoice's own FAQ hedges:** background wake-word "is controlled by the operating system, and
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5678-  Picovoice **cannot guarantee** that this will be possible in future releases of iOS."
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5679-- Every phone call, Siri invocation, or app grabbing the mic is an interruption you must catch and
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5680-  recover from — and recovery is not always granted. User swipes the app away → dead, nothing
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5740-  `workspace`, `tools` profile, `identity`. All four providers natively supported:
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5741-  - **Codex** — supported, but a distinct runtime path (`codex` plugin + native app-server harness). Fiddliest of the four; budget real time.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5742-  - **Grok/xAI** — supported; SuperGrok OAuth is the documented recommended path (subject to the tier trap above).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5743-  - **Ollama** — supported, auto-detected at `127.0.0.1:11434`.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5744:  - **Claude headless** — supported via `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` (reuses `claude -p` under your own session auth). This is the escalation seat.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5745-- **The dispatcher** = native subagents (`sessions_spawn`). Non-blocking, returns a run id,
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5746-  and **each spawn takes an explicit `model` param** — so one orchestrator turn fans out across
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5747-  Grok + Ollama + Claude simultaneously. `maxConcurrent` default 8; `maxSpawnDepth` 2 is the
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5748-  documented orchestrator pattern. **Do not build a custom dispatcher.**
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5890-## 6. Ranked recommendations
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5891-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5892-**Adopt as-is**
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5893-- OpenClaw core, **pinned to an exact version** — seats as `agents.list[]`, `codex` plugin for the
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5894:  orchestrator, `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` for the Claude seat.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5895-- Native subagents for dispatch (`maxSpawnDepth: 2`, per-spawn `model` override).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5896-- `autoreview` skill as the gauntlet spine.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5897-- `openclaw gateway install` (launchd) + Tailscale Serve auto-config.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5898-- **Pipecat** (BSD-2) as the voice framework; `kokoro-onnx` via `pipecat-ai[kokoro]` for TTS;
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5916-- calimero (severity × agreement-count aggregation).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5917-- clu (SQLite atomic claiming, checkpoints).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5918-- `claude-to-codex` / `ccode-to-codex` — **take the mapping spec, hand-write the ~200 lines.** Both
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5919-  are experimental (`claude-to-codex` self-describes as *"primarily vibe-coded"*, 6★) and **silently
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:5920:  drop hooks, `maxTurns`, and memory settings.** Our agent definitions are the actual product —
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5921-  don't run an unvetted converter over them. Note the non-obvious effort remap
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5922-  (`high`→`xhigh`, `medium`→`high`).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5923-
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-5924-**Ignore**
--
