docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6024-- Every phone call, Siri invocation, or app grabbing the mic is an interruption you must catch and
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6025-  recover from — and recovery is not always granted. User swipes the app away → dead, nothing
--
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6085-  `workspace`, `tools` profile, `identity`. All four providers natively supported:
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6086-  - **Codex** — supported, but a distinct runtime path (`codex` plugin + native app-server harness). Fiddliest of the four; budget real time.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6087-  - **Grok/xAI** — supported; SuperGrok OAuth is the documented recommended path (subject to the tier trap above).
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6088-  - **Ollama** — supported, auto-detected at `127.0.0.1:11434`.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out:6089:  - **Claude headless** — supported via `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` (reuses `claude -p` under your own session auth). This is the escalation seat.
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6090-- **The dispatcher** = native subagents (`sessions_spawn`). Non-blocking, returns a run id,
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6091-  and **each spawn takes an explicit `model` param** — so one orchestrator turn fans out across
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6092-  Grok + Ollama + Claude simultaneously. `maxConcurrent` default 8; `maxSpawnDepth` 2 is the
docs/sol/sol_family_floor_task10.out-6093-  documented orchestrator pattern. **Do not build a custom dispatcher.**
--
