docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-350-### ⚠️ The landmine — this kills the Claude Max head, and possibly the whole subscription premise
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-351-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-352-**CLI-based runtimes cannot be in a per-turn voice loop:**
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-353-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:354:- `claude -p` subprocess: **3–5s overhead per call.** Cited discussion says this makes "use cases
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-355-  like voice assistants **prohibitively slow**."
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-356-- Claude Agent SDK `query()`: **~12s overhead per call**, no hot-process reuse
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-357-  ([claude-agent-sdk-typescript#34](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript/issues/34)).
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-358-- With process pre-warming/reuse: drops to <1s. Without it, you eat the full cost **every turn**.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-359-- Direct Messages API: 1–3s end-to-end.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-360-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:361:This collides head-on with the constraint from §1: **`agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` is the only
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-362-*legal* way to use the Claude Max subscription (Anthropic bans subscription OAuth in third-party
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-363-tools) — and it is exactly the path that costs 3–5s per turn.**
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-364-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-365-> **You cannot have both "Claude Max subscription" and "snappy voice head." They are mutually
--
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-383-  agentic tool-calling, no CoT overhead, subscription already held — *but its TTFT is unverified and
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-384-  load-bearing*); (2) **Claude Haiku 4.5** via direct API (~1.04s, best TTFT consistency — needs API
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-385-  billing, not the Max sub); (3) **GPT-5.6 at `none`/`low` effort** (OpenAI's own guidance names
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-386-  `low` for latency-sensitive work — but same family as the 13s number, so verify).
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:387:- **Explicitly NOT the head:** GPT-5.6-sol at high/max, Claude Fable, **anything behind `claude-cli`.**
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-388-- **Dispatch targets (Reasoners):** GPT-5.6-sol high/max via Codex; Claude Opus/Fable via
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:389:  `claude-cli`; Grok Build; Ollama. All spawned non-blocking via `sessions_spawn` with explicit
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-390-  per-spawn `model`. Their multi-second startup is irrelevant in the background.
