docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-474-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-475-### Other things that bite
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-476-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-477-- **Hard 60-minute session cap.** A 2-hour builder session needs ≥2 reconnects with context
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:478:  rehydration — and a fresh session means a **cold cache** (cost spike + a memory seam). Needs
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-479-  design, not hand-waving.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-480-- **Prompt caching is load-bearing, not an optimization.** Without it the context-replay term goes
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-481-  from $0.168/hr → **$13.44/hr**. That is the entire difference between "cheap" and "unusable."
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-482-  Requires a stable prefix — never interpolate timestamps into the system prompt.
--
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-585-Chief is not one thing with one access level. He's **three layers**, each with
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-586-different permissions:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-587-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-588-1. **Voice/chat LLM** — the thing that talks to you. Reads a system prompt
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:589:   you've seen (agent roster, memory files, project context). Runs on the
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-590-   Anthropic API. Has no hands.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-591-2. **Voice/chat LLM with project-switch detection** — same LLM, but the
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-592-   server-side handler can update `current_project` based on your
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-593-   utterance. That's the most it can change.
--
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-596-   is the layer with real hands. Full filesystem write within the scoped
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-597-   repo. Full git. Full `gh`. Full pytest. Full anything you have installed.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-598-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-599-The security story is that **layers 1 and 2 are read-only + routing**, and
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:600:**layer 3 is scope-gated + env-restricted**. Everything interesting lives at
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-601-layer 3.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-602-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-603----
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-604-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-605-## Layer 1: Voice/chat LLM (read-only, always-on)
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-606-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-607-### Reads
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-608-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:609:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user/memory/*.md` (your global user + feedback
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:610:  memory, always loaded)
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:611:- `~/.claude/agents/memory/*.md` (Chief's own agent roster — Atlas, Forge,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-612-  Riggs, Finn, Nova, Vera, Hawke, Sable, Pax, Quill, Hip, names + roles)
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:613:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user-Desktop-<scope>/memory/*.md` (**only** the
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:614:  currently-scoped project's memory, exact canonical match, no substring
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-615-  leaks)
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-616-- Conversation history within the current WebSocket session
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-617-- Project scope set via the picker or voice command
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-618-
