docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-783-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-784-Two options we're evaluating for direct-write capability:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-785-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:786:1. **`append_to_memory(scope, filename, content)` tool** — Chief voice has
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-787-   a bounded tool that appends to scope-matching `.md` files. Scope-gated
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:788:   (can't write Arch memory while scoped to Chief Command). No path
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-789-   traversal, no creation of new filenames outside a whitelist pattern.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-790-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-791-2. **Dispatch everything.** Memory edits go through `claude` subprocess,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-792-   meaning a full audit trail + ability to review edits before they land.
