docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1198-Full detail in `docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md`. The load-bearing ones:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1199-
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1200-- **The Claude credit pool does not exist.** Anthropic announced it, then *paused it
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1201:  before it took effect*. `claude -p` draws on normal subscription limits today. The cap
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1202-  in `seats.toml` is forward-proofing, not a current necessity.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1203-- **Codex parallel workers: 6, not 8.** `max_threads` defaults to 6.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1204-- **Codex OAuth is tolerated, not sanctioned.** No OpenAI doc blesses it, and both other
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1205-  major vendors closed this exact door within five months. Keep the API-key swap ready —
--
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1262--- Seats: the named roles from spec §4. Providers are swappable behind these.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1263--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1264-CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS seats (
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1265-    id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- 'brain' | 'workhorse' | 'grinder_local' | 'reviewer' | 'tester' | 'mouth'
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1266:    provider      TEXT NOT NULL,             -- 'codex' | 'xai' | 'ollama' | 'claude-cli' | ...
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1267-    model         TEXT NOT NULL,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1268-    -- Model FAMILY, not provider. Two seats can share a family via different providers
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1269:    -- (e.g. claude-cli and an Anthropic API key are both 'claude'). The gauntlet's
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1270-    -- diversity rule and the no-self-testing guard both key off this, so it must be
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1271-    -- the thing that actually determines shared blind spots.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1272-    family        TEXT NOT NULL,             -- 'gpt' | 'claude' | 'grok' | 'qwen'
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1273-    -- tier drives the review guard below. 'local' output is never trusted on its own.
--
