docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1326:-- Projects: the top-level thing work belongs to. Each has its OWN memory.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1327---
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1328:-- Owner: "ability to see a projects tab and each project has its own memory,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1329--- timeline/planning."
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1330---
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1331--- This matters more than it looks. Memory that isn't scoped to a project leaks:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1332--- lessons from the EMR bleed into the harness, conventions from one codebase get
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1333:-- applied to another. Chief already keeps per-AGENT memory; this is per-PROJECT,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1334--- and the two are different axes. Riggs knows how HE works; the project knows how
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1335--- IT works.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1336--- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
