docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1429-    -- 'done'    = the gauntlet passed. The machine is satisfied.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1430-    -- 'shipped' = NEILL said it works on his device. Only he can move this.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1431-    -- These are NOT the same thing, and conflating them is how agents launder
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:1432:    -- confidence. From Chief's memory, learned the hard way:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1433-    --     "Chief must NEVER say 'shipped' unless Neill has confirmed it works on
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1434-    --      his device. 'Shipped' is reserved for Neill-confirmed-working."
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1435-    -- That rule now lives here instead of in a prompt.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-1436-    status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'todo'
