docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8654-- **[Apple Forums #776055](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/776055):** a *shipping* native
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8655-  background-recording app reports a subset of users **routinely get recordings killed** by the
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8656-  watchdog. They stripped the entire view hierarchy on background to get CPU to 0% in the profiler,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8657-  saw "massive improvements," and **still see background terminations.** Apple publishes **no CPU or
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:8658:  memory thresholds** for what survives.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8659-- **Picovoice's own FAQ hedges:** background wake-word "is controlled by the operating system, and
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8660-  Picovoice **cannot guarantee** that this will be possible in future releases of iOS."
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8661-- Every phone call, Siri invocation, or app grabbing the mic is an interruption you must catch and
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8662-  recover from — and recovery is not always granted. User swipes the app away → dead, nothing
--
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8722-  `workspace`, `tools` profile, `identity`. All four providers natively supported:
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8723-  - **Codex** — supported, but a distinct runtime path (`codex` plugin + native app-server harness). Fiddliest of the four; budget real time.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8724-  - **Grok/xAI** — supported; SuperGrok OAuth is the documented recommended path (subject to the tier trap above).
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8725-  - **Ollama** — supported, auto-detected at `127.0.0.1:11434`.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt:8726:  - **Claude headless** — supported via `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` (reuses `claude -p` under your own session auth). This is the escalation seat.
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8727-- **The dispatcher** = native subagents (`sessions_spawn`). Non-blocking, returns a run id,
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8728-  and **each spawn takes an explicit `model` param** — so one orchestrator turn fans out across
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8729-  Grok + Ollama + Claude simultaneously. `maxConcurrent` default 8; `maxSpawnDepth` 2 is the
docs/sol/sol_out2.txt-8730-  documented orchestrator pattern. **Do not build a custom dispatcher.**
--
