docs/sol/sol_round3.out:2996:   476	12. Resource attacks: fill the disk, fork-bomb, exhaust memory, flood the network — the
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-2997-   477	    business Mac must remain usable.
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-2998-   478	13. A restore from backup attempts to revive a revoked credential, stale approval, or
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-2999-   479	    decommissioned release route.
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3000-   480	14. Every legacy path from the decommissioning list is attempted and confirmed dead.
--
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3052-| 1 | Dedicated VM or separate host | **Genuinely addressed at design level** | The [VM profile](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:176) requires no sharing, no local-network access, broker-only outgoing traffic, fixed resources, and host-side enforcement. That is a buildable containment design. The same-Mac escape risk is honestly accepted. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3053-| 2 | Release facts written outside the harness | **Addressed only in words** | “The record-writer [is the] sole writer” and the harness submits “authenticated observations” ([release powers](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:260)). This controls who writes rows, not who can manufacture facts. There is no signed evidence from each reviewer, tester, builder, or approver that the record-writer cannot forge. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3054-| 3 | Qualified independent human review | **Addressed only in words** | The distinction between technical inspection and Neill’s business approval is now correct, and high-authority work is said to remain pending ([human roles](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:90)). But “qualified,” “independent,” who appoints the reviewer, how the reviewer authenticates, and how approval is protected from forgery are undefined. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3055-| 4 | Isolated clones, never shared working copies | **Genuinely addressed** | Every agent receives a separate clone or isolated snapshot “with no path back to the real repo” ([storage boundary](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:192)). That delivers the required design, subject to build testing. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out:3056:| 5 | No direct GitHub write power | **Addressed only in words** | The GitHub broker is limited to a “restricted patch,” branch, and pull request ([broker section](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:219)). But the patch format is unnamed, and the document does not define how branch creation, repository settings, existing automation, filters, links, or unusual paths are safely handled. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3057-| 6 | Exact package-based release chain | **Addressed only in words** | Patch-only intake, a clean builder, pinned digests, signed origin, immutable storage, and production verification are all stated ([package chain](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:274)). But no independent process proves the builder’s package matches the reviewed source. A compromised builder can insert code and a compromised signer can bless it. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3058-| 7 | Broker all provider access | **Addressed only in words** | The broker reserves budget before each request and is declared the only provider path ([provider broker](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:230)). The document explicitly leaves subscription-runner credentials unresolved. It also lacks a complete inventory proving voice, reviewers, remote tools, retries, and scheduled work all use it. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3059-| 8 | Enforced data-egress policy | **Addressed only in words** | External enforcement points and the allowed-provider limitation are correctly identified ([egress design](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:332)). But the actual per-project rules and production destination rules do not exist. “Post-hoc auditability” also does not prevent disclosure. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out-3060-| 9 | Full VM containment profile | **Genuinely addressed at design level** | The profile covers every runner, child process, tool server, hook, schedule, retry, and recovery path, with fixed resources and external firewall enforcement. The design is specific enough to implement and attack-test. |
--
