docs/chief-access-model.md-14-Chief is not one thing with one access level. He's **three layers**, each with
docs/chief-access-model.md-15-different permissions:
docs/chief-access-model.md-16-
docs/chief-access-model.md-17-1. **Voice/chat LLM** — the thing that talks to you. Reads a system prompt
docs/chief-access-model.md:18:   you've seen (agent roster, memory files, project context). Runs on the
docs/chief-access-model.md-19-   Anthropic API. Has no hands.
docs/chief-access-model.md-20-2. **Voice/chat LLM with project-switch detection** — same LLM, but the
docs/chief-access-model.md-21-   server-side handler can update `current_project` based on your
docs/chief-access-model.md-22-   utterance. That's the most it can change.
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-25-   is the layer with real hands. Full filesystem write within the scoped
docs/chief-access-model.md-26-   repo. Full git. Full `gh`. Full pytest. Full anything you have installed.
docs/chief-access-model.md-27-
docs/chief-access-model.md-28-The security story is that **layers 1 and 2 are read-only + routing**, and
docs/chief-access-model.md:29:**layer 3 is scope-gated + env-restricted**. Everything interesting lives at
docs/chief-access-model.md-30-layer 3.
docs/chief-access-model.md-31-
docs/chief-access-model.md-32----
docs/chief-access-model.md-33-
docs/chief-access-model.md-34-## Layer 1: Voice/chat LLM (read-only, always-on)
docs/chief-access-model.md-35-
docs/chief-access-model.md-36-### Reads
docs/chief-access-model.md-37-
docs/chief-access-model.md:38:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user/memory/*.md` (your global user + feedback
docs/chief-access-model.md:39:  memory, always loaded)
docs/chief-access-model.md:40:- `~/.claude/agents/memory/*.md` (Chief's own agent roster — Atlas, Forge,
docs/chief-access-model.md-41-  Riggs, Finn, Nova, Vera, Hawke, Sable, Pax, Quill, Hip, names + roles)
docs/chief-access-model.md:42:- `~/.claude/projects/-Users-user-Desktop-<scope>/memory/*.md` (**only** the
docs/chief-access-model.md:43:  currently-scoped project's memory, exact canonical match, no substring
docs/chief-access-model.md-44-  leaks)
docs/chief-access-model.md-45-- Conversation history within the current WebSocket session
docs/chief-access-model.md-46-- Project scope set via the picker or voice command
docs/chief-access-model.md-47-
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-57-  defaults stay cheap because heavy lifting moves to layer 3.
docs/chief-access-model.md-58-
docs/chief-access-model.md-59-### Risks
docs/chief-access-model.md-60-
docs/chief-access-model.md:61:- **Prompt injection from memory files.** Memory files are concatenated into
docs/chief-access-model.md-62-  the system prompt. A compromised sub-agent writing to one could hijack
docs/chief-access-model.md-63-  Chief's behavior. Mitigation: identity-prompt guard text, provenance
docs/chief-access-model.md:64:  fences around each file (`<memory file="…" mtime="…">…</memory>`), and
docs/chief-access-model.md-65-  file-source tagging so odd instructions are visible.
docs/chief-access-model.md:66:- **Symlink read.** Someone dropping a symlink at `~/.claude/.../memory/`
docs/chief-access-model.md-67-  to `~/.ssh/id_rsa` would get it read into Chief's context and sent to
docs/chief-access-model.md-68-  Anthropic. Mitigation: symlink rejection at read time (implemented in
docs/chief-access-model.md:69:  `memory_paths.safe_md_files` + `team_service`/`memory_service`).
docs/chief-access-model.md-70-
docs/chief-access-model.md-71----
docs/chief-access-model.md-72-
docs/chief-access-model.md-73-## Layer 2: Project-switch detection
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-77-- The user's utterance (text or STT transcript)
docs/chief-access-model.md-78-
docs/chief-access-model.md-79-### Writes
docs/chief-access-model.md-80-
docs/chief-access-model.md:81:- The in-memory `current_project` variable for the WS session
docs/chief-access-model.md:82:- In-memory `_context_store` keyed by JWT subject (persists across tabs)
docs/chief-access-model.md-83-
docs/chief-access-model.md-84-### Executes
docs/chief-access-model.md-85-
docs/chief-access-model.md-86-- `detect_project_switch` regex match against the user text
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-211-## What Chief voice itself can write (future v1.1)
docs/chief-access-model.md-212-
docs/chief-access-model.md-213-Two options we're evaluating for direct-write capability:
docs/chief-access-model.md-214-
docs/chief-access-model.md:215:1. **`append_to_memory(scope, filename, content)` tool** — Chief voice has
docs/chief-access-model.md-216-   a bounded tool that appends to scope-matching `.md` files. Scope-gated
docs/chief-access-model.md:217:   (can't write Arch memory while scoped to Chief Command). No path
docs/chief-access-model.md-218-   traversal, no creation of new filenames outside a whitelist pattern.
docs/chief-access-model.md-219-
docs/chief-access-model.md-220-2. **Dispatch everything.** Memory edits go through `claude` subprocess,
docs/chief-access-model.md-221-   meaning a full audit trail + ability to review edits before they land.
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-229----
docs/chief-access-model.md-230-
docs/chief-access-model.md-231-## What Chief CANNOT do (today and v1.1)
docs/chief-access-model.md-232-
docs/chief-access-model.md:233:- Read files outside `~/.claude/projects/…/memory/` and `~/.claude/agents/memory/` (layer 1)
docs/chief-access-model.md-234-- Write any file at layer 1 or 2
docs/chief-access-model.md-235-- Run shell commands at layer 1 or 2
docs/chief-access-model.md-236-- Access GitHub unless you explicitly add the token to the allowlist
docs/chief-access-model.md-237-- Access AWS / cloud providers
--
docs/chief-access-model.md-247-  tasks can push PRs? If yes, should we add a per-repo validation wrapper?
docs/chief-access-model.md-248-- **Desktop beyond-repo access:** any case where a task should be able to
docs/chief-access-model.md-249-  touch files in `~/Desktop/` outside its scoped repo? (Probably no, but
docs/chief-access-model.md-250-  worth explicit.)
docs/chief-access-model.md:251:- **Direct memory write:** should Chief voice be able to append to memory
docs/chief-access-model.md-252-  files directly (option 1 above), or only via dispatch (option 2)?
docs/chief-access-model.md-253-- **Auto-suggest scope switch on implicit cross-project mention:** ship
docs/chief-access-model.md-254-  in v1.1?
docs/chief-access-model.md-255-
