docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out-3789-   125	// pool. It does NOT — Anthropic announced that, then PAUSED it before it took effect.
docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out:3790:   126	// `claude -p` runs on normal subscription limits TODAY. Claude-as-workhorse would not
docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out-3791-   127	// cost extra dollars.
docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out-3792-   128	//
docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out-3793-   129	// ✅ THE REAL REASON, which nobody had written down: RATE LIMITS, not cost. Running a
docs/sol/sol_real_code_builders.out-3794-   130	// workhorse hard (unattended overnight builds, migrations, backfills) burns Max plan
