docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-385-+# Reviewing lives in gauntlet.py (task #10). This module builds; that one judges.
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-386-+# It used to hold a single hard-wired Claude reviewer, which was enough to close the
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-387-+# loop and was never the design — one reviewer cannot show that a DIFFERENT MIND looked.
--
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-472--    """A stronger model to check the local work — a Claude seat (its own login, no
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-473--    metered key involved), so the loop can close without touching anything that still
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-474--    needs rotating."""
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-475--    row = c.execute(
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt:476:-        "SELECT id FROM seats WHERE provider = 'claude-cli' AND enabled = 1 ORDER BY id LIMIT 1"
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-477--    ).fetchone()
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-478--    return row["id"] if row else None
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-479-+# Who reviews is NOT the server's decision any more (task #10). It used to hand-pick a
docs/sol/review_task10_gauntlet_bundle.txt-480-+# single Claude seat here, which quietly made "one reviewer" the real policy no matter
--
