   285	def start_in_background(job_id: int, *, cfg: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> threading.Thread:

codex
The decisive missed issue is not the diff hash. It is execution: the in-flight tester runs builder-authored test code as the owner, inside a linked worktree, before merge. That gives unreviewed code the same access to the owner’s secrets, live record, gatekeeper token, and shared Git control files that the proposed builder itself has. A passing review cannot undo damage that happens during the test run.
